meta {
  name: Purge — Account acct-1001
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

delete {
  url: {{invalidatorUrl}}/cache/entity/Account/acct-1001
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  THE invalidation demo. Deletes every cached response tagged with this
  account, in both tag directions, so no dangling tags are left behind.

  Demo flow:
    1. Run "Account full portfolio"  -> MISS, REST called
    2. Run it again                  -> HIT, no REST traffic
    3. Run "Fund by ID"              -> caches an unrelated response
    4. Run this purge                -> ~16 keys deleted, across 2 operations
    5. List all cache keys           -> only the Fund response survives
    6. Run "Account full portfolio"  -> MISS again, fresh data

  This endpoint talks straight to Valkey. It imports nothing from Hive, which
  is the point: your REST services can trigger it when data changes.
}
